WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.120
Hey, I'm Michael Koka, Head of Digital Commerce at Revolution Nutrition.

00:00:10.120 --> 00:00:14.720
I scaled our Amazon channel

00:00:14.720 --> 00:00:18.758
from zero to tens of millions in annual revenue in just two years.

00:00:18.758 --> 00:00:20.000
Everything I'm sharing comes

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:20.912
from real execution.

00:00:20.912 --> 00:00:21.824
Let's dive in.

00:00:21.824 --> 00:00:24.560
Today I want to talk about what actually drives

00:00:24.560 --> 00:00:25.914
sustainable growth on Amazon.

00:00:25.914 --> 00:00:28.960
One of the biggest lessons sellers learned is that

00:00:28.960 --> 00:00:31.618
traffic alone doesn't scale a business.

00:00:31.618 --> 00:00:32.505
Systems do.

00:00:32.505 --> 00:00:34.720
Start by nailing operations early.

00:00:34.720 --> 00:00:40.640
Make sure fulfillment, inventory planning and forecasting are solid before pushing aggressive

00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:41.157
marketing.

00:00:41.157 --> 00:00:47.360
Stockouts kill momentum and hurt a ranking, so availability really matters more

00:00:47.360 --> 00:00:49.255
than most people realize.

00:00:49.255 --> 00:00:53.520
Approach advertising with purpose, don't just spend, structure campaigns

00:00:53.520 --> 00:00:57.943
around your product life cycle, launch, ranking, then profitability.

00:00:57.943 --> 00:01:00.400
Separate branded and non-branded

00:01:00.400 --> 00:01:06.352
campaigns optimize using real search key terms and consistently cut wasted spend.

00:01:06.352 --> 00:01:07.840
Another major growth

00:01:07.840 --> 00:01:09.714
lever is repeat customers.

00:01:09.714 --> 00:01:14.400
Think about bundles, promotions, subscribe and save and your overall

00:01:14.400 --> 00:01:15.800
post purchase experience.

00:01:15.800 --> 00:01:20.000
Increasing lifetime value makes scaling far more sustainable than

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:22.160
chasing one-time buyers.

00:01:22.160 --> 00:01:23.780
Finally, expand strategically.

00:01:23.780 --> 00:01:26.480
Don't launch everything at once.

00:01:27.040 --> 00:01:33.920
Scale asin by asin so each product gets proper attention, inventory support and optimization.

00:01:33.920 --> 00:01:37.280
Real growth on Amazon comes from consistency.

00:01:37.280 --> 00:01:39.680
Small weekly improvements across operations,

00:01:39.680 --> 00:01:50.133
advertising and customer experience compound faster than most sellers expect.
